From 3ac1375ee7af902467994c2b5897f2fd079541eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brhett <36874370+jingledingle521@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:44:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 46/47] Finder: keep slow work off the GUI thread; cheaper
 repaints

The cloud drive poll checked the mount with QStorageInfo every 2 seconds.
That statfs()es the rclone mount, and rclone answers it with a call to
Google every 5 minutes, which took more than 3 seconds, so the window
froze. Read /proc/self/mountinfo instead. The once-a-minute quota call
now waits 30 seconds instead of hanging up after 3, which cancelled it
every time ("context canceled" in the mount's log).

AirDrop no longer blocks the window: stopping the peer lookup doesn't
wait up to 2 seconds for it to exit, and the receiver's PID is looked up
in the background, not with a blocking systemctl twice a second.

Repaints: the sidebar caches tinted icons, and its sync spinner redraws
only the cloud rows. The window background finds the status bars every
half second, not by walking the widget tree on every paint. The size
formatter compiles its regex once, and the view repaints for zebra
stripes only when it has them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
